CORE
main.c
--datarace --no-assertions --no-por --unwind 5 --rounds 2
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^split small choices: 1$
^path bounds: [1-9][0-9]* branches decided$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Each thread picks a slot with a random j >= 0 and walks the slots from j to 3,
incrementing the cell each slot points to (a pointer read from slot[j]).
The walk is split into one copy per value 0..3 of j; in the leftover case the
path says j >= 0 and j is none of 0..3, so the loop test j < 4 is decided
false and the loop is not built.
